WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.983
- Hi, everyone.

00:00:00.983 --> 00:00:01.890
I'm Carolina.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.280
I love everything movies, I
love everything pop culture,

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.200
and I'm the type of person
that when I watch movies,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.060
I look at a kitchen and I go ugh,

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.230
I wish that was my kitchen.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.360
Specifically, Nancy Meyer kitchens, okay?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.180
So today, we're gonna
be taking this kitchen

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.070
and we're gonna be
transforming it into the style

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.630
of three of my favorite movies.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.660
One, of course, being a Nancy
Meyers film, It's Complicated.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.800
The second being Amelie,

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.660
and the third, Howl's Moving Castle.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.970
Now listen, I can't decorate
this space by myself.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.670
Luckily, we have an amazing
group of women today,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.100
we have Alyssa and Claire on the art team,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.960
they're gonna be transforming this space,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.760
and I can't wait to
see what it looks like.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.590
Now let's get to our first kitchen.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.803
Nancy Meyers, I hope I make you proud.

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:40.805
(clapboard snapping)

00:00:40.805 --> 00:00:41.638
So the first kitchen we have today

00:00:41.638 --> 00:00:43.230
is inspired by the movie It's Complicated.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.740
It is a 2009 film by Nancy
Meyers starring Meryl Streep,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.970
Alec Baldwin, Steve Martin.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.890
A great cast of people, dare I say?

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.470
So when I first heard we
were doing a video like this,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.900
I immediately thought we have
to do Nancy Meyers kitchen,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.733
hello?

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:57.570
That's the best parts of
her films are her sets,

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.880
her kitchens, and allegedly,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.370
her own kitchen is quite
beautiful and spectacular.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.250
Nancy, please invite me over
so I can verify that statement.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.340
But it was one of those movies
that was on HBO all the time,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.690
so when my mom would watch it,

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.040
I would just sit and watch it with her.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.090
I was way too young,

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.890
way too young to be watching this movie.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.690
However, I loved it!

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:19.140
I love Nancy Meyers films so
much, The Parent Trap, hello?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.230
It's the best movie ever,
and this movie in particular,

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.450
my favorite scene is when Meryl Streep

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.800
is making the chocolate croissants.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.480
My mom and I talk about that scene a lot,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.340
we've even attempted to
make chocolate croissants

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.730
and it just was not up to par.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.380
Everything here in the
kitchen, for the most part,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.213
is pretty neutral.

00:01:35.213 --> 00:01:36.660
The movie is set in Santa Barbara

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.260
so this aesthetic is the
coastal grandmother aesthetic.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.570
You might've remembered it
as being a TikTok trend,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.970
people were calling it also
the Nancy Meyers aesthetic.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.630
Flowy white T-shirts,
some not so skinny jeans,

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.700
maybe some of those new cute mini Uggs,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.570
you know what I'm talking about?

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.460
You know maybe you're
drinking your hot coffee

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.130
or your hot chocolate and you're
looking out onto your beach

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.870
and you're just like
contemplating your life,

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.180
that's the kind of aesthetic
we were going for today.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.520
So contrary to the
title, It's Complicated,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.250
and the messy love triangle
that we see in the film,

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.750
the kitchen is not complicated.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.360
It's very clean, it's very
much where Meryl Streep

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.970
has full control of her life,
whereas everywhere else,

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.500
she kinda does not. (laughs)

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.700
This kitchen in particular,

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.550
has everything a baker/chef
needs within reach.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.190
The food is all on display,
it's in glass coverings,

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.380
it's in eyesight so you
know you're in a very good,

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.490
ready to eat kitchen.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.860
So it's a lot of rattan vibe.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.170
Now, as much as I love
a good coastal kitchen,

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.120
it's time to swipe this kitchen away,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.043
and into the world of a fun,
Parisian Amelie kitchen.

00:02:34.043 --> 00:02:34.876
(clapboard snapping)

00:02:34.876 --> 00:02:36.866
Bienvenue to Amelie's kitchen!

00:02:36.866 --> 00:02:40.200
Who can forget that iconic scene
of her in the movie theater

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.420
where she's just looking
straight into the camera,

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.070
and then she looks back at the people?

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.690
Amelie is a movie that has left

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.880
such a huge impact in my life.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.250
I feel like it's an animated
film for some reason,

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.360
that's what it comes across.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.193
And the colors!

00:02:52.193 --> 00:02:53.760
I mean who could forget the colors?

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.530
The colors are so unique.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.480
The greens, the reds, the yellows,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.920
and they're all inspired by paintings

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.690
of Brazilian artist, Juarez Machado.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.250
Now, the character of Amelie is someone

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.170
who doesn't really need lavish things.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.930
All of her decor is very
simple, it's very traditional,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.640
she likes to bake so we have things

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.080
that are easy access to bake.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.090
Now, the clock is such an
important motif in the film

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.980
because the narrator, whenever
he narrates something,

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.570
there's always a specific time attached

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.560
to whatever is going on.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.930
So it's smack dab in the
center of the kitchen.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.810
Now in the film Amelie, she
has a windowsill of plants

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.960
and herbs so she can spy on
her neighbors, like I do also,

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.810
and we paid homage to that
with these little plants

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:28.890
at the edge of the sink.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.470
Now, Amelie also has a cat,
if you remember the scene

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.090
where she thinks her lover

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.060
is gonna come through the
beaded doorway and it's the cat,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.140
and I also have a cat.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.435
So we paid homage to the
cats by having the paintings

00:03:39.435 --> 00:03:41.910
and the little statue above the microwave.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.160
Now, Amelie loves to
bring joy to strangers

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.750
with the gnome in the film,

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.460
so we also have our own little gnome

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.380
that'll bring joy every
time we enter the kitchen.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.790
Now this kitchen, like the film,

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.320
is all about the little details,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.990
specifically in the coloring
with the red and the greens

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.100
like I mentioned before.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.210
So we have red tables, we
have green and red utensils,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.340
some mugs, and to bring out some texture,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.840
we have some checkered things as well.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.900
And I mean this table is so
cute and it's so reminiscent

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.970
of the tables of the
cafe where Amelie works.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.260
Now, as much as I love this kitchen,

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:12.840
it's time to say au revoir to Montmartre

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.480
and hello to Miyazaki.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.819
(clapboard snapping)

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.760
Now last but certainly not least,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.780
is the recreation of Howl's
Moving Castle in kitchen form.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.180
Now, I am so excited
about this transformation,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.190
specifically because Studio Ghibli films

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.350
have left such a huge impact on my life,

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.940
especially Howl's Moving Castle.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.420
This is just very earthy, it
feels kinda human, if you will,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.120
with the heart right
there, very cluttered.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.710
And it is very cluttered at
the beginning of the film

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.380
until Sophie comes and
cleans it all up for him.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.380
So the kitchen is inside a
really weird, big moving castle,

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.460
hence the title, Howl's Moving Castle,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.096
and so it's very much
human, it's very cluttered.

00:04:50.096 --> 00:04:52.140
If the house is moving,
things are gonna shift,

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.150
things are gonna be messy,
and if you've seen the film,

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.200
you're probably like wait,

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.390
I know that little plate back there.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.780
So this plate is a callback
to the portal door situation

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.150
in Howl's Moving Castle where
he gets to different places,

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.050
if you will.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.300
So it's a painted plate
as a callback to that,

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.133
how cute is that?

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.750
One really awesome thing
about Studio Ghibli movies

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.070
is the food.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.810
The ASMR food I think is an aspect

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.700
in every single film of his.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.820
When Sophie first enters the
castle, there's food everywhere

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.980
because they can't
really cook without Howl

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.650
telling Calcifer what to
do, but Sophie's like no,

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.630
I'm gonna do it, I'm gonna
boss Calcifer around.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.480
Now, one of my favorite
scenes in Howl's Moving Castle

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.790
is when Howl gets mad at Sophie

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.410
'cause she messes with his potions

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.330
so he picks the wrong one
and his hair changes color,

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.610
and I like when Howl
has his dark hair, okay?

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.300
So as an ode to all the
magic potions in the castle,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.940
we have the little bottles
right here, super cute.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.790
What feels so special
about this kitchen is,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.730
within a moving castle, it's
very human, it's very DIY,

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.770
it's not immaculate, it's not clean.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.415
Like humans, it's messy.

00:05:51.415 --> 00:05:52.576
(clapboard snapping)

00:05:52.576 --> 00:05:53.649
And there you have it!

00:05:53.649 --> 00:05:54.990
That was such an
incredible transformation.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:56.790
Comment below which of the transformations

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.860
was your favorite, and which
of your favorite movies

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.000
has the best kitchen,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.653
and maybe we'll get to do it next time?

00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:02.486
(dinging effect)

00:06:02.486 --> 00:06:03.319
Thanks for watching, bye!

00:06:04.377 --> 00:06:07.044
(upbeat music)

